    "ver": "0.35.0",
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Comfy UGC - 2 Speech take\n\n**Speech take (a speaker's first take)** (8.7 s): the creator speaks the take's lines with H3's own voice, starting and ending on the keyframe stills. Model: fl2va (first/last-frame model: the text encoder also sees both stills). Speed: 8-step turbo LoRA.\n\n**Take 1 of the spec**\n1. \"Okay, real talk, most magnesium I tried did nothing for me.\"\n2. \"So I stopped guessing and started reading labels.\"\n\n**How to use**\n1. Make the stills first (**1 Keyframe stills**) and set them on **FIRST FRAME** and **LAST FRAME** (the preloaded ones are samples). Every object the take moves must be visible and within reach in the first frame.\n2. Group 1: **HQ?** on (default) = HQ 768x1376, the approved look (a 15 s speech take is about $0.44); off = draft 576x1024 for quick tests.\n3. Group 0: the **PROMPT** comes from `take_graph.py --print-prompt` (MiniMax's own caption format). Edit it in the same style: describe only what is seen and heard, no negations ('nothing floats' makes things float), spoken words only inside `<d>[English] ...</d>` after `(S1)`. Change **SEED** to re-roll.\n4. Run, then check it with **5 Review (Gemini QA)** and by eye and ear.\n\n**Preloaded**: take 1 prompt, seed, sample stills, size (576x1024 draft / 768x1376 HQ), length 209 frames (17k+5 grid at 24 fps).\n\n**Turbo LoRA**: `minimax_h3_fl2v_turbo_8step_v1.0_comfyui_bf16.safetensors` (Comfy Cloud catalog)\n\n**Not in this workflow (runs locally in the skill)**\nSpend guard, the lint (`take_graph.py --lint`), upload of stills and downloading the file: `take_graph.py --submit` does them. In the UI you press Run yourself (it costs credits).\n\n**License**: the H3 community license excludes US/EU/UK/KR use, outputs included. Tests only until the client has a license from MiniMax.\n\nSource: `scripts/ui_build.py` in the repo. Edit here in the UI, then run `scripts/ui_sync.py pull \"<name>\"` and the agent updates the skill to match."
   ],
   "title": "Read me"
  }
 ],
